1
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:13,340
Try lightening up on peace
and stepping away from it, okay?

2
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:26,880
Aiming for a day floating on the Nakagawa,

3
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:34,000
I kick a pebble and my shoe flies off too.

4
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:42,300
Onto the head of the carpenter
who had been saving up,

5
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed that I was still just a brat.

6
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I somehow stir
up some energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,620
pachinko, a single yawn, nothing changes.

8
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:02,520
The streetscape feels strangely kind.

9
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,500
From the pointy hat's water bottle,

10
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:16,800
the sunset sinks toward the corner shop.

11
00:01:20,910 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow too, it'll end just like this

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,400
Katsushika Shibamata,
once again, even happiness is lost.

13
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,840
Because I'm a fool who only
realized it when I listened.

14
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,480
Even imagined feelings are part of love.

15
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,600
Alright, it's finished!

16
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:49,960
Finished, he says?

17
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:51,000
It's not a kotatsu.

18
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,180
It's not just any kotatsu.

19
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:55,140
Just get in without asking questions.

20
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:58,280
You didn't rig it with some weird trap,
did you?

21
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:00,840
You can let your legs hang down.

22
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:03,880
So there's a hole in the floor here.

23
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:06,820
Well? This is a sunken kotatsu!

24
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:10,020
I bought it at the electronics
store's winter clearance sale.

25
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:13,020
I couldn't very well cut a hole in the second floor of the dorm,
could I?

26
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:15,200
So this is a sunken kotatsu?

27
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:17,500
Well, it's easier on the legs, at least.

28
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:18,040
Really.

29
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:21,700
Back in the day, I used to hide in
spots like this during hide-and-seek.

30
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:24,880
True, a few kids could fit in there.

31
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:26,580
But here's the thing.

32
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:31,580
It wasn't electric.
We used briquettes and coal.

33
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:34,080
After all, we burned the charcoal
right there under the table.

34
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:36,220
The inside of the kotatsu is sealed off,
you know.

35
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:39,880
If you stay in there too long,
you get carbon monoxide poisoning.

36
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:44,220
Once, everyone hiding in there passed out,
and it turned into a huge commotion!

37
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:46,920
Yeah, I really thought we
were going to die that time.

38
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:47,720
Well...

39
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,560
That's dangerous, you know.

40
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:53,660
Ever since we switched to electric heaters like now,
we don't have to worry about that.

41
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:58,360
Well then, we're off on patrol.

42
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:00,100
I'm heading over to the station for a bit.

43
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:02,120
Ryo-chan,
please watch the place while we're gone.

44
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:02,780
Yeah.

45
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:18,040
Oops, oops. It was so warm I dozed off.

46
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:23,820
Damn. I forgot to tighten the screws.

47
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,080
It's dangerous if it moves, you know.

48
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:28,520
Let's make sure to tighten them properly.

49
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,080
Thanks a lot for giving me a ride.

50
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:37,760
No, it's on my way anyway.

51
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,800
Why don't you stop by for a bit?

52
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,980
Ryo-chan built a horigotatsu.

53
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:43,220
It's nice and warm.

54
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:45,420
Wow, really?

55
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:47,900
This is my first time using a horigotatsu.

56
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:49,620
Me too.

57
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:53,880
Says the one whose country home still
has a horigotatsu to this day, right?

58
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:59,420
How about this man, for example?

59
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:02,320
He works at the town office.
He's serious and a good person.

60
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:04,160
Ugh, Mom.

61
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,560
I told you, I have no intention
of getting married for a while.

62
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,780
You really are a troublesome girl.

63
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:11,800
You're the only daughter in the
village who hasn't married yet.

64
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,280
Oh no, oh no.

65
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:16,160
My sophisticated city-girl
image is going to be ruined!

66
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,300
What's wrong, Komachi?

67
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:19,460
It's nothing.

68
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:21,420
I said I'd try making a horigotatsu too,
for the first time.

69
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:23,400
I'm so excited!

70
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,000
There, that's good.

71
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:27,120
Wow, it's real!

72
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,800
So this is a horigotatsu

73
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:29,960
Go on, get in and try it!

74
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:31,040
It's warm in here, isn't it!

75
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:31,380
Uh-oh.

76
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:36,180
It's so warm~

77
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:38,480
At least your legs don't go numb, right?

78
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,540
Really.

79
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:40,820
Well, this is a problem.

80
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:43,000
I can't get out of here now.

81
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:45,020
Can't be helped.

82
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:46,960
I'll stay like this until
Reiko and the others leave.

83
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:52,100
There's something like a
scrub brush inside the kotatsu.

84
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:53,560
A scrub brush?

85
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:54,680
Oops.

86
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:55,480
Where?

87
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:57,980
It really is!

88
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,860
But it's kind of warm, you know?

89
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:02,140
So maybe it's a scrub-brush-like cat?

90
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:03,740
That's creepy!

91
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:04,980
No way!

92
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:07,960
Enough already!

93
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:08,500
Aaah!

94
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,960
Ryotsu Kankichi!

95
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:12,120
So you were hiding inside, you pervert!

96
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:15,900
No! If I were tightening the heater's screws,
you'd be the one who got hurt!

97
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:19,080
No excuses! Enemy of women, Skewfen!

98
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:19,980
Wait a second!

99
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:22,340
Cockroach, Hairena, Zani, Gechigechi!

100
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:24,100
What are you, you meddling little brat!

101
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:25,500
Uyaaa!

102
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:26,920
Uya!

103
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,240
Huh, hmph, hmph.

104
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:33,260
Komachi, you've been getting way too worked up over Ryo-chan lately,
haven't you?

105
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:36,240
Even I can't keep up with you, honestly.

106
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:39,860
Hmph! This perverted
gorilla should just disappear!

107
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:43,040
Damn you, Komachi!

108
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:51,020
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes found it. Yes.

109
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:52,660
Mom.

110
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:57,200
I was wondering how things
are going with Ryo-san.

111
00:05:57,200 --> 00:06:00,680
Don't be ridiculous, nothing's going
to happen with a weirdo like that.

112
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,640
You don't need to be embarrassed.

113
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:06,680
When he came home with you the other day, it
looked like things had gotten pretty far along.

114
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:09,020
I keep telling you, that's not it.

115
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:11,260
I was just talking about it with Dad.

116
00:06:11,260 --> 00:06:13,600
He'd suit country living, too.

117
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:16,620
Maybe he should come
back here and settle down.

118
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:19,640
This is pointless, I'm hanging up.

119
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,340
You're completely mistaken.

120
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:27,080
When it comes to Ryo-san,
she really gets worked up.

121
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:31,340
Did she get that from me, the way she says the
opposite of what she feels when she's embarrassed?

122
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:34,400
There's no doubt Komachi likes Ryo-san.

123
00:06:34,940 --> 00:06:36,860
The question is what Ryo-san thinks.

124
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:42,280
Alright, I'll go to Tokyo myself and
find out Ryo-san's feelings directly.

125
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:43,800
That's a good idea, dear.

126
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:47,580
If Ryo-san comes over here,
we won't have anything to complain about.

127
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:48,820
Leave it to me.

128
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:09,400
Someday, surely, a prince on a
white horse will come to rescue me.

129
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:19,680
Prince...

130
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:24,120
Ahhhhh! Komachi, I have come to rescue you!

131
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:26,720
Now, come into my arms.

132
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:28,160
Ahhhhh!

133
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:31,720
Eeeeeeh!

134
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:40,260
Ahhhhh! What a dream!
This is a nightmare beyond all limits.

135
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:43,840
That Kankichi Ryotsu as my prince?
The worst thing in my whole life.

136
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:53,420
With this disguise, Ryo-san won't notice me.

137
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:55,860
Right, time to start the
investigation right away.

138
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:59,180
Ryo-san?

139
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:02,280
That man is the picture of health.

140
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:05,340
Even if he fell out of a plane
or got hit by a bullet train,

141
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:07,040
he's always as lively as ever.

142
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:11,700
I see, so his body is healthy
and there's no worry about illness.

143
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:15,620
Well, you could say he's
still a wild animal at heart.

144
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:22,320
Hey, country living suits him perfectly. Once he gets into something,
he can't stop, that's him.

145
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:31,080
He stays up all night building plastic models.
He's so dedicated and hardworking, he's a perfect match for you.

146
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:38,180
I had a strange dream, so I've felt awful all day.
There's a fortune-telling that's really accurate, you know.

147
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:43,560
To cheer myself up, I could have my future marriage partner read.
Maybe I'll do that.

148
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,320
I see it, I see it!

149
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,580
You, in a wedding dress,

150
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:52,800
Really?

151
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:55,600
The one standing beside you is

152
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,620
what kind of person?

153
00:08:56,780 --> 00:09:00,120
Tall, handsome, rich,
and he even has a Ferrari.

154
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:02,180
That's Nakagawa, isn't it?

155
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:03,600
Shut up!

156
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:05,040
So, what kind of person is he?

157
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:08,480
Centipede-like eyebrows,

158
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:10,940
short, shaved-back hair,

159
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:14,040
and a strong, square jaw,

160
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:14,600
Stop it!

161
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:16,260
Open mouth!

162
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:16,860
Eeeh!

163
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:19,980
Murky eyes with no restraint,
shut your mouth!

164
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,620
Pee-yah!

165
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:32,940
That's exactly Kankichi Ryotsu, isn't it?

166
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:34,600
N-no, that's a lie!

167
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:38,280
Whether you believe it or not is up to you.

168
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:38,753
But,

169
00:09:38,803 --> 00:09:43,860
the first man you meet after
leaving here is exactly that person.

170
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,000
That's all lies.

171
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,460
It's obviously nonsense.

172
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:57,920
But everyone says this
place is always right.

173
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:59,900
She's just talking out of her neck.

174
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:00,880
Komachi.

175
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:03,460
What are you doing?

176
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:06,140
What are *you* doing?

177
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:07,380
Komachi.

178
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:09,420
R-Ryo... Kankichi Ryotsu?

179
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:11,420
The first man I meet...

180
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:13,100
N-no, that's not...

181
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:17,560
Aaaah! Why is that perverted
gorilla wandering around here?

182
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:20,260
What are you talking about?
You're the one who ran into me!

183
00:10:20,260 --> 00:10:21,800
Found it! Mom!

184
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:24,880
What's with this noisy girl!

185
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:25,920
What is this?!

186
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:27,560
You bastard!

187
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:29,220
Shut up!

188
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:32,860
Look at them,
carrying on so cozily in broad daylight!

189
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:36,780
Alright, all that's left is
to find out how Ryo-chan feels.

190
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:44,280
Ugh, how stupid! I'll head home
and have a drink to clear my head.

191
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,460
Ryo-san, are you going all-in
on one pick again this time too?

192
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:58,420
I can't think of anyone but her, after all.

193
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:01,100
Komachi's my top pick.

194
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:03,680
Welcome!

195
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,400
What can I get you?

196
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:07,840
A hot sake, please.

197
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:09,300
One hot sake!

198
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:12,260
Is she really that good?

199
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:16,180
Well, she's a bit fiery,
but we get along great.

200
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:18,740
Yeah, definitely.

201
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,660
We're a real perfect match, you could say.

202
00:11:24,460 --> 00:11:25,500
That's right.

203
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:27,680
Her legs when she's
running are impressive too,

204
00:11:27,680 --> 00:11:30,000
but those moist eyes of
hers are irresistible.

205
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:42,140
You like Komachi too

206
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:44,340
Of course I do.

207
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:45,680
I fell for her at first sight.

208
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:47,560
I'm betting on her, I tell you.

209
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:50,280
Good, as long as that's clear, I'm all set.

210
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:52,660
They say customers should eat it while it's hot,
after all.

211
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:54,420
You're too happy-go-lucky.

212
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:56,100
I'll treat you, on the house.

213
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:59,080
What's up with that guy?

214
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:01,300
Does he really like her that much?

215
00:12:02,220 --> 00:12:03,920
Sakura Komachi, there's no helping it.

216
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:18,140
Eeeeeh!

217
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:19,860
That Komachi, you...

218
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:21,000
Really?

219
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:21,700
Yes.

220
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:24,500
She's definitely a woman, right?

221
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:26,140
Of course.

222
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:27,100
Well, obviously.

223
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:29,360
Right, isn't she?

224
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:31,800
Her measurements are...

225
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,840
Bust 83, cup C.

226
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:35,700
Waist 58, hips 88.

227
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:40,660
83 C

228
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:42,920
Why are you getting so worked up?

229
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:46,240
There's really no mistake.

230
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:54,860
Komachi and me, we're a match made in mutual love.
We couldn't ask for a better couple! Aaaah!

231
00:12:55,320 --> 00:13:00,400
If I could marry Komachi, I'd give anything, even for free.
It's like a dream, Mom.

232
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:09,140
Kankichi getting married? Then shall we proceed with the arrangements?
Hey, this isn't a joke either.

233
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:11,420
Let's throw a big party and go all out!

234
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:17,800
Hey, come on, don't joke around so much.

235
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:19,840
Marry that creep?

236
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:22,980
So that fortune-teller was right after all.

237
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:24,860
What do you mean, Naoko?

238
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:26,940
That's Komachi's father, isn't it?

239
00:13:26,940 --> 00:13:29,680
You know,
these things are better done sooner.

240
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:31,360
Your mother too, about you...

241
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:32,360
Enough already!

242
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:35,520
I absolutely hate that perverted gorilla!

243
00:13:36,260 --> 00:13:37,480
No need to be shy.

244
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:39,500
They say hating someone is
just loving them in disguise.

245
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:44,600
So you like Komachi too

246
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:46,980
Of course.
I fell for her the moment I saw her.

247
00:13:46,980 --> 00:13:48,860
I'm betting on this one, I tell you.

248
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:51,960
Whoa, he's confessing his love!

249
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:53,560
No way.

250
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:55,400
I'll tell you as many times as you like.

251
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:56,980
That's it.

252
00:13:56,980 --> 00:13:58,160
I fell for her at first sight.

253
00:13:58,160 --> 00:14:00,160
I fell for her at first sight.

254
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:02,220
I fell for her at first sight.

255
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:03,960
Stop it.

256
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:05,620
Big news!

257
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:07,860
Ryotsu Kankichi confesses
his love to Komachi!

258
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:08,820
Heading toward marriage!

259
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:15,280
Ryo-chan and Komachi-chan
are getting married?

260
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:16,640
No way.

261
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:21,140
Please, please, let us be the
matchmakers for the couple's wedding.

262
00:14:21,140 --> 00:14:23,540
We humbly ask the Chief for this favor.

263
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:27,420
In that case, we'll take it on.

264
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:30,240
With this,
Ryo will leave the station's jurisdiction,

265
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:33,580
and if he moves to the countryside,
nothing could be more welcome.

266
00:14:35,220 --> 00:14:37,460
So Ryo-san is finally getting married.

267
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:42,000
I hear the bride's family owns a lot of
mountain and farmland in the countryside.

268
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:45,120
Maybe we can get him to pay back
his debts with the wedding gifts.

269
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:47,840
That psycho Ryo-san, of all people.

270
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:51,340
We'd better throw a big farewell party!

271
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:55,960
Ryo-san

272
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:57,920
What on earth happened?

273
00:14:57,920 --> 00:15:01,080
Word on the street is that
you and I are getting married.

274
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:03,160
It's your fault.

275
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:06,220
Just because I'm young, cute, and sexy,

276
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:09,240
you confessed that you're smitten with me!

277
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:13,120
What? I don't remember ever saying that!

278
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:17,260
But it's recorded on tape.
You said you fell for me at first sight.

279
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:18,520
That's ridiculous!

280
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:22,500
So you like Komachi too

281
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:25,392
Right. You're the customer
from the bar that time.

282
00:15:25,442 --> 00:15:29,400
She must have misunderstood when
I said I liked Sakura Komachi-ō.

283
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:31,980
Sakura Komachi-ō?

284
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:32,824
It's a horse.

285
00:15:32,874 --> 00:15:36,820
I'd much rather have a racehorse
than a wild filly like you.

286
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:43,200
You're one to talk, Centipede Monster! Centipede
Monster?! Where on earth am I a centipede?

287
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:49,340
You've got eyebrows like a centipede,
so you're the Centipede Monster. Got it?

288
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:55,420
Insulting someone over their appearance is so childish,
Komachi-kun.

289
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:58,260
Hey, hey, you two lovebirds!
It's getting hot in here!

290
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:01,260
Did you two come here to
pick out wedding rings?

291
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:03,060
I'm so jealous.

292
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:04,380
Right?

293
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:08,980
We won't get in your way.

294
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:10,460
See you two.

295
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,420
It's not like that, Sakonji.

296
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:16,380
What are we going to do?
We've been misunderstood again!

297
00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:18,860
Shut up! That guy jumped to
conclusions all on his own.

298
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:21,340
If you hadn't come here,
this wouldn't have happened!

299
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:23,400
It's always your fault, isn't it?

300
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,440
Don't talk nonsense, Komachi.

301
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,840
It's not nonsense!

302
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:30,320
The fact that you were here,
and that you know Sakonji,

303
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:32,220
it's all your fault!

304
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,160
Hey, are you even listening?

305
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:37,780
This is no time for that, Komachi!

306
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:41,000
Hey!

307
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:44,100
Let me take a look inside that box.

308
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:48,140
What on earth were you
doing in this jewelry store?

309
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:48,340
Hey!

310
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,320
Don't move!

311
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:55,180
Now that you've seen this,
you're coming with us.

312
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:03,720
The two of them are buying wedding rings?

313
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,720
Colonel and Ryotsu are
out of the running too

314
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:12,000
So the senior is finally putting
an end to his long bachelor life.

315
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,900
If that's true, we really ought
to throw him a big celebration.

316
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:19,500
What did you just say?

317
00:17:19,820 --> 00:17:22,840
Those guys are the wanted jewel theft gang.

318
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:24,000
There's no doubt about it.

319
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:24,960
I see.

320
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:28,320
I thought I'd seen them somewhere...
so it was from the wanted notices.

321
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:32,880
If that's the case,
they'll definitely kill us to keep us quiet.

322
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:35,020
We have to get out of here quickly.

323
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,740
No, no, that won't do.

324
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,420
The groom, Ryotsu-kun,

325
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:47,940
is a model police officer loved by everyone,

326
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:53,200
and has the most reprimand letters, not just
in the precinct but in the whole country.

327
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:56,020
He even ranks first in the
"men you'd never want to marry" category.

328
00:17:56,020 --> 00:17:57,180
This won't do, this won't do.

329
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:59,420
That doesn't even sound like praise.

330
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,560
I never realized how hard
it is to praise that man.

331
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:09,540
Boss, that went off without a hitch.

332
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,140
That was close.

333
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:13,180
What about the two behind us?

334
00:18:14,140 --> 00:18:18,140
Hey, you're going to fall into
a ravine along with this car!

335
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:21,860
What are you doing?

336
00:18:21,860 --> 00:18:23,960
I'm just trying to untie the rope.

337
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:26,940
Liar! You touched me in all the confusion!

338
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:28,880
Who'd ever touch your butt?

339
00:18:29,420 --> 00:18:30,100
Fine, I get it!

340
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:32,720
Nobody's touching anyone!
We don't have time for this!

341
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:34,760
Untie this rope, quick!

342
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:38,339
That good-for-nothing
is my biggest headache,

343
00:18:38,389 --> 00:18:40,160
No, my pride and joy...

344
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:47,280
Writing such blatant
lies makes my hand shake!

345
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:54,900
Looks like we've wandered
onto a mountain path.

346
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:56,800
We have to do something,
or we're seriously in trouble!

347
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:59,040
What do we do? We can't untie the rope.

348
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:00,620
For now, let's stand up.

349
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:04,940
No good, no good.
I just can't think of anything.

350
00:19:04,940 --> 00:19:06,300
One, two, three!

351
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:07,600
We did it!

352
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:11,540
We're totally busted, this is bad.

353
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:12,700
Serves you right.

354
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:15,920
You did that on purpose just now,
didn't you?

355
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:18,680
You idiot! Who would do something
like that at a time like this?

356
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:27,660
Did you just hear a voice?

357
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:30,780
There are lots of tanuki and foxes around here,
you know.

358
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:36,580
Komachi, don't move your feet apart.

359
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:38,820
Easy for you to say.

360
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:41,500
It's no use, I've reached my limit.

361
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:42,540
Hang in there!

362
00:19:42,540 --> 00:19:45,620
Listen, rub the rope against
the road surface to cut it.

363
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:54,800
Yay!

364
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:58,220
Thanks.

365
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:01,860
Alright, time to strike back!

366
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:04,420
Heave-ho!

367
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:07,060
Komachi, you stay here.

368
00:20:07,060 --> 00:20:10,360
No way! We have to pay back
those guys who did this to us.

369
00:20:10,360 --> 00:20:11,680
Fine, it can't be helped.

370
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:15,560
One, two, go!

371
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:18,320
A tunnel!

372
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:19,320
Get down!

373
00:20:29,980 --> 00:20:30,780
Got it?

374
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:32,440
This is nothing.

375
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:34,480
You're pretty reliable, aren't you.

376
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:35,960
Alright, let's go.

377
00:20:43,260 --> 00:20:44,240
Listen, Komachi.

378
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:47,520
On one, two, three,
we jump in from the right and the left.

379
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:52,620
Leave it to me! When we were little,
we always played Taa-chan together!

380
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:54,740
Alright, let's go!

381
00:20:55,380 --> 00:20:56,460
One, two...

382
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:56,720
Three!

383
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:09,920
Alright! That's enough!

384
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:11,580
Don't move!

385
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:14,860
You went and hurt our comrades.

386
00:21:15,360 --> 00:21:17,620
Not that I was planning on
keeping you alive anyway.

387
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:20,080
You're going to die right here.

388
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:32,900
Saved us there, Komachi.

389
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:36,420
A cliff!

390
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:37,760
Brakes!

391
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:39,100
Yay!

392
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:53,100
Komachi, are you all right?

393
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:54,780
I-I'm fine.

394
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:03,260
Ugh, w-what is this feeling?

395
00:22:04,300 --> 00:22:07,820
Not bad at all.
I've got a new respect for you, you know.

396
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:10,560
My heart's pounding for some reason.

397
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:14,940
Well, let's pick up the
thieves and head back.

398
00:22:14,940 --> 00:22:16,740
This is a major achievement!

399
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:27,420
Yay!

400
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:29,780
Yay!

401
00:22:31,340 --> 00:22:31,900
Yay!

402
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:34,560
Yay!

403
00:22:35,580 --> 00:22:36,380
Yay!

404
00:22:36,700 --> 00:22:37,020
Yay!

405
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:40,320
Great work, great work!

406
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:42,100
Ryo-chan finally did it

407
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:44,420
Congratulations, Komachi.

408
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:45,280
Thank you.

409
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:48,380
Alright, lower the curtain!

410
00:22:48,380 --> 00:22:48,760
Curtain?

411
00:22:53,720 --> 00:22:54,720
W-what?

412
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:59,220
We thought the quicker route would
be best for this sort of thing.

413
00:22:59,220 --> 00:23:02,380
Everyone was happy to lend us a hand!

414
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:04,220
Come on, Komachi-chan, hurry up!

415
00:23:04,220 --> 00:23:05,000
This way.

416
00:23:06,460 --> 00:23:07,600
And now, we shall begin.

417
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:08,716
Ryotsu, Ono,

418
00:23:08,766 --> 00:23:12,460
we will now hold the wedding
reception hosted by both families.

419
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:14,740
Go for it, Kankichi!

420
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:16,140
Come on, knock it off, you.

421
00:23:16,140 --> 00:23:18,200
Congratulations, Komachi.

422
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:19,560
W-what, that's...

423
00:23:20,160 --> 00:23:23,960
Why do I have to marry this harpy?

424
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:25,080
Did you just call me a harpy?

425
00:23:26,420 --> 00:23:30,100
Well, you're a mountain woman. You were good at climbing since you were a kid,
weren't you?

426
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:37,280
What was that, you perverted gorilla?

427
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:38,780
What did you say, you little hellion?

428
00:23:39,900 --> 00:23:40,760
I've been waiting for that!

429
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:49,000
You short-fused, short-eating,
single-celled caveman!

430
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:52,660
You're a mountain woman,
a rice-guzzling glutton!

431
00:23:52,660 --> 00:23:58,840
I hate you! I hate you! I hate you!
I hate you! I can't stand you!

432
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:22,240
Surprise and commotion,
solving together, and quick resolution

433
00:24:22,660 --> 00:24:25,340
and helping, anticipating

434
00:24:26,060 --> 00:24:29,400
Dun-dun, decided, and inspiration strikes

435
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:32,320
bouncing along and wrapping up

436
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:35,320
and action, flying off

437
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:40,080
More than anything, an amazing power

438
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:45,960
If everyone gathers and comes here

439
00:24:46,900 --> 00:24:52,220
the final energy, like a dream

440
00:24:53,540 --> 00:24:59,620
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday,
painting the sky, standing on the ground

441
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:03,440
The star of Kameari,
Ryo-san, is just the same

442
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:07,080
This should be fine, right?

443
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:08,560
Of course it's not fine!

444
00:25:22,660 --> 00:25:23,660
Thank you for watching.

